window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"The Thracia Peninsula has two faces.","2":"The northern half is a land of rich grassy plains, divided among many small kingdoms,","3":"while the southern half, among its harsh mountains and barren earth, holds the kingdom of Thracia, known for its dragon knights.","4":"Thracia, known for its reckless valor,","5":"had repeatedly invaded in the past to seize the rich northern lands,","6":"but had failed again and again against the resistance of the Leonster royal family.","7":"It seemed that annihilating Leonster's army in the Yied Desert had finally achieved that long-held ambition,","8":"but then Prince Bloom of House Friege conquered this region with his great host,","9":"and ever since, it had remained under the Empire's control as the Kingdom of North Thracia.","10":"From then, for over a decade, even the ambitious King Travant","11":"found himself utterly unable to act against the Empire's military might,","12":"and a strange peace was maintained.","13":"But the Liberation Army's capture of the capital, Alster,","14":"upset the delicate balance of this region.","15":"Alster Castle and Leonster Castle were now held by Celice's Liberation Army,","16":"while at Conote Castle, King Bloom, having fled from Alster, gathered troops,","17":"and at Manster Castle, Princess Ishtar, known by the epithet Thunder God,","18":"stood firm in her defenses against Thracia,","19":"while in Thracian-held Miloah, King Travant,","20":"together with his front-line commander General Mycoff, kept an uncanny silence.","21":"The people's one and only wish was","22":"that this land would once again return to the rule of the Leonster royal family.","23":"And now, the curtain rose on a new battle.","24":"(Bloom): Damn those rebels... getting too pleased with themselves.","25":"(Bloom): Vampa, even you three have come running back — I didn't expect that of you.","26":"(Fetra): My deepest apologies. But there's no need to worry anymore.","27":"(Fetra): General Muhamado's forces are already on their way to Alster,","28":"(Fetra): and General Ovo's knights are advancing on Leonster — we too will set out right away.","29":"(Bloom): I see... I'm counting on you. By the way, that King Travant of Thracia — what's he doing? Is he still not coming to help?","30":"(Fetra): Yes, we've sent requests for reinforcements many times, but...","31":"(Bloom): Damn it... what is that fellow thinking...","32":"(Fetra): King Travant is an ambitious man — trusting him seems dangerous to me...","33":"(Bloom): You're right. Even without borrowing his strength, we can crush the rebels on our own.","34":"(Bloom): Vampa, Fetra, Elu, go. This time, bring me their heads for sure!","35":"(Fetra): Yes sir, without fail!","36":"(Villager (man)): Lady Sety, when on earth will Manster return to our own hands?","37":"(Villager (man)): We're suffering under King Bloom's rule — we're at our limit!","38":"(Sety): Don't give up hope. Lord Celice's Liberation Army is almost here.","39":"(Sety): Please tell everyone to hold on just a little longer.","40":"(Sety): Freedom will surely come. Please, trust me!","41":"(Arion): Father, King Bloom has asked for our aid.","42":"(Arion): It seems the Empire has lost Leonster Castle and Alster Castle to the rebels.","43":"(Travant): That brat they call Celice, Sigurd's little whelp...","44":"(Travant): For Bloom to struggle against a mere child like that, has he grown senile? Arion, just leave them be.","45":"(Travant): Let the Empire and the rebels wear each other down fighting, and our Thracian army will strike when both sides are weakened.","46":"(Arion): I thought as much... father, are you still thinking about that time...","47":"(Travant): How could I ever forget!","48":"(Travant): I buried the knights of Leonster in the desert, and thought I had finally achieved the conquest of the Thracia Peninsula,","49":"(Travant): and then that Bloom snatched it right out from under me. Even now, I haven't forgotten that fury.","50":"(Arion): We don't have the strength to face Grannvale head-on... father, I understand how you feel.","51":"(Travant): Unifying the Thracia Peninsula is our people's long-cherished dream. To save our people from poverty, we need that rich northern land.","52":"(Travant): We've been scorned as hyenas,","53":"(Travant): and even so, the only way we've managed to survive is by hiring ourselves out to fight for other nations.","54":"(Travant): Arion, I've endured this for a long time. But now is the time to rise up.","55":"(Travant): Thracia's fate will be decided in this one battle — remember that.","56":"(Arion): Yes sir...","57":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, something feels off — is Leonster's defense really secure?","58":"(Celice): I can't say it's fully sufficient. Should we send reinforcements?","59":"(Levin (Strategist)): Mm, I doubt King Bloom of Conote will just sit idle after this.","60":"(Levin (Strategist)): And besides, the people of Manster are asking for help too — the sooner we move, the better.","61":"(Celice): Understood. Let's set out at once.","62":"(Muhamado): Don't fear the rebels! Take back Alster Castle.","63":"(Muhamado): Anyone who disobeys orders will be beheaded, understand! Kill them all!","64":"(Ovo): Alright, preparations are complete. Let's race straight to Leonster — don't let General Muhamado's unit get ahead of us!","65":"(Fetra): At last, it's begun. Fetra, Elu, let's go. Don't mess it up again this time.","66":"(Fabal): King Bloom, you need something from me?","67":"(Bloom): Ah, Fabal, glad you came. I've been waiting.","68":"(Fabal): I'm a busy man. If you need something, out with it!","69":"(Bloom): Ugh... well... it's nothing much, but I'd like you to do a little job for me.","70":"(Fabal): A job...?","71":"(Bloom): Mm, I need your help suppressing the rebels.","72":"(Fabal): I refuse... I'm a mercenary, but I don't do dirty work.","73":"(Bloom): But you need money, don't you. I hear you're taking care of a great many orphans.","74":"(Bloom): And your sister needs money too, doesn't she — stealing for it, from what I hear. Are you content letting your sister be a thief?","75":"(Fabal): Patty is... pushing herself for the children's sake... money... I certainly do need it...","76":"(Bloom): Then there's nothing to hesitate about. Bring me Celice's head, and I'll give you as much gold as you like — your sister will be pleased too.","77":"(Fabal): ...understood. It's a foolish thing, but there's no helping it... this once, I'll lend you a hand.","78":"(Ishtar): Father, you called for me? What do you need?","79":"(Bloom): Ah, Ishtar, you've finally come. The Liberation Army is attacking — I need your strength. Protect me.","80":"(Ishtar): I can hardly believe you'd say such a thing, father. Mere rebels, and you're this flustered?","81":"(Bloom): But listen — your brother Ishtore has already been struck down, and we've lost Tinny too, on top of it.","82":"(Bloom): The three Vampa sisters can't be relied on either. All that's left is to borrow your strength.","83":"(Ishtar): Understood. In that case, give me the Thoron Hammer.","84":"(Ishtar): With that alone, I can wipe out the enemy single-handedly.","85":"(Bloom): Wh-, what? The Thoron Hammer...? Hmm, very well... take it. But make absolutely sure you succeed.","86":"(Ishtar): I understand. Leave it to me.","87":"— (only if Ishtar is still alive)","88":"(Julius): Ishtar, come back with me to Belhalla. You mustn't die in a place like this.","89":"(Ishtar): Ah, Lord Julius... but, why...","90":"(Julius): I need you. Lend me your strength.","91":"(Ishtar): Y-, yes! Gladly... Lord Julius.","92":"(Julia): Lord Celice...","93":"(Celice): Julia? What's wrong?","94":"(Julia): I feel something terrifying... I sense an evil presence drifting somewhere nearby.","95":"(Celice): Huh? What do you mean?","96":"(Julia): .........Celice, be careful... Ishtar is a terrifying enemy... you mustn't fight her...","97":"(Celice): Julia!? ...what's wrong!!","98":"(Julia): Huh... I... what did I just...","99":"(Celice): Julia... you...","100":"(Finn): Prince Leaf, we have a duty to protect this region.","101":"(Finn): It will be a hard fight, but please bear with it.","102":"(Leaf): I know that already. I've long dreamed of this very day coming.","103":"(Leaf): Saving the people from King Bloom's tyranny and restoring peace to the Thracia Peninsula — this is also my late father's will.","104":"(Leaf): Even if I vanish like the morning dew on some battlefield, I have no regrets.","105":"(Finn): Prince Leaf,","106":"(Finn): a man who will one day be king shouldn't speak so carelessly about such things!","107":"(Leaf): You're right, I'm sorry. You protected and raised me through the Empire's harsh pursuit when I was still small.","108":"(Leaf): Going without food yourself, you never once let me go hungry.","109":"(Leaf): Only now do I truly understand how difficult that must have been. Finn, I really am grateful to you.","110":"(Finn): Prince Leaf, unifying the Thracia Peninsula, torn by endless war, was your father's lifelong dream.","111":"(Finn): Please, carry on your father's will — you are the only one left who can.","112":"(Arthur): Fee, be careful. Just because you can fly doesn't mean you should go off alone.","113":"(Fee): Oh my, Arthur — are you worried about me?","114":"(Arthur): W-, well... I suppose...","115":"(Fee): Hmm...","116":"(Fee): I always thought you weren't interested in other people, Arthur... but it turns out you have a kind side too.","117":"(Fee): I've reconsidered my opinion of you, just a little.","118":"(Arthur): You're special, Fee...","119":"(Fee): Eh...?","120":"(Arthur): Anyway, don't do anything too dangerous! See you...","121":"(Fee): Arthur...","122":"(Vampa): Damn... these rebels...","123":"(Muhamado): To think we'd be defeated so easily... King Bloom, forgive me...","124":"(Ovo): Not bad at all... but it ends here!","125":"(Pamela): Th-, that can't be...","126":"(Fetra): Take this! Elfire!!","127":"(Fetra): Ahh, how regrettable... Fetra, Elu...","128":"(Vampa): Take this! Elwind!!","129":"(Vampa): Damn... these rebels...","130":"(Elu): Take this! Elthunder!!","131":"(Elu): Vampa, Fetra... this is the end...","132":"(Fabal): I'm sorry... this is for the money too...","133":"(Fabal): Patty... forgive your brother...","134":"(Patty): Big brother!? What are you doing in a place like this!","135":"(Patty): Don't tell me you've been hired by Bloom!","136":"(Fabal): Patty? Why are you with the rebels!?","137":"(Patty): To help everyone, of course. We're all joining our strength together to beat King Bloom.","138":"(Patty): Big brother, have you forgotten? The children's parents were killed by the imperial army.","139":"(Patty): And you're cooperating with that very same army — big brother, what on earth are you thinking!","140":"(Fabal): Patty... I'm sorry... you're right... I... I don't know what got into me.","141":"(Patty): Anyone can say they're sorry. If you really mean it, then lend your help too, big brother — let's bring back peace, all of us together!","142":"(Fabal): Alright, Patty. But you, you've changed quite a bit, haven't you...","143":"(Patty): Heh... well, maybe...","144":"(Fabal): Prince Celice, I'm sorry. Please forgive me.","145":"(Celice): You must be Fabal. I heard the story from Patty.","146":"(Celice): It sounds like there were various circumstances involved. I don't hold it against you.","147":"(Fabal): No, I was in the wrong. To let myself be hired by the Empire, what a foolish thing to do... I'm ashamed of myself.","148":"(Fabal): Prince Celice, let me make up for it.","149":"(Celice): Thank you, Fabal. I'll be counting on you.","150":"(Fee): Phew, we've come up quite high. I wonder where my brother could be. Mana, are you alright? Can you still fly?","151":"(Fee): You're named after that aunt of mine, the hero known throughout Silesse — this much shouldn't be enough to wear you down, right?","152":"(Fee): Once things are peaceful, let's go back to Silesse together.","153":"(Fee): Or else... heh, maybe I'll go off to marry some wonderful person.","154":"(Fee): Either way, I need to do my best a little longer!","155":"(Villager (man)): Oh, a person! We're saved!!","156":"(Linda): What's wrong?","157":"(Villager (man)): Ah, I set out on a journey hoping to join the Liberation Army, but I got lost on the way...","158":"(Villager (man)): How'd you end up in a place like this, in these mountains?","159":"(Linda): I'm fighting for peace, together with Lord Celice.","160":"(Villager (man)): So you really are with the Liberation Army! Hah, to think I'd meet someone from the Liberation Army in a place like this...","161":"(Villager (man)): I hate to admit it, but I'd lost my nerve and was just about to head back to the village.","162":"(Villager (man)): My sweetheart Anna must be worried too...","163":"(Linda): I see... I wish we could have fought together...","164":"(Villager (man)): Well, I'm just a shooter, so I can barely move around on the battlefield anyway.","165":"(Villager (man)): Even if you'd let me join, I'd probably have just held everyone back.","166":"(Villager (man)): That's right, could you tell me your name?","167":"(Linda): My name is Linda.","168":"(Villager (man)): Linda? That name sounds familiar somehow.........","169":"(Villager (man)): Well, never mind — here, I'll give you this ward charm. I don't need it anymore.","170":"(Linda): Thank you...","171":"(Villager (man)): Well then, good luck — may Naga's blessing be with you!","172":"(Villager (man)): Oh, a person! We're saved!!","173":"(Amid): What's wrong?","174":"(Villager (man)): It's a long story, but a lot has happened...","175":"(Villager (man)): I got lost on the way, and a girl from the Liberation Army named Linda helped me out,","176":"(Villager (man)): but I hate to admit it, here I am lost again.","177":"(Amid): I see. Linda is my little sister. I'm Amid — if there's anything I can do, let me help.","178":"(Villager (man)): Wait, so you're... Linda's big brother!","179":"(Villager (man)): Hah! To think I'd meet you of all people here... ...how embarrassing...","180":"(Amid): Don't be so down on yourself, it's alright now. Come along with me for a while — if an enemy appears, just hide behind me.","181":"(Villager (man)): ...you're a good person... and both you and your sister, too...","182":"(Amid): When we're in trouble, we help each other out, that's all.","183":"(Villager (man)): ...you're a good person, really a good person...","184":"(Villager (man)): Here, I'll give you a ward charm too — actually, I happened to have another one, just in case... heh heh.","185":"(Amid): Is that so? Then I'll gratefully accept it.","186":"(Villager (man)): Alright then, once I get back home, Anna and I will make kids just like you two!","187":"(Amid): Before that, we need to cross this mountain — come now, let's go.","188":"(Villager (man)): Wait just a moment! I don't have much movement range, you know!","189":"(Ishtar): I'm sorry... but you'll have to die! Thoron Hammer!!","190":"(Ishtar): Ahh... Lord Julius...","191":"(Julius): Ishtar, come back with me to Belhalla. You mustn't die in a place like this.","192":"(Ishtar): Ah, Lord Julius... but, why...","193":"(Julius): I need you. Lend me your strength.","194":"(Ishtar): Y-, yes! Gladly... Lord Julius.","195":"(Bloom): Damn it... what on earth is happening... you rebels... I'll never forgive you!","196":"(Bloom): Guh... how regrettable...","197":"(Levin (Strategist)): It seems the Empire's power here has finally run its course. The remaining soldiers, hearing of Conote's fall, seem to have fled.","198":"(Celice): Then Manster's liberation should be realized soon too.","199":"(Levin (Strategist)): I'd like to think so. The problem is Thracia...","200":"(Celice): But Thracia has maintained neutrality. I don't think they'd turn against us.","201":"(Levin (Strategist)): You can say that because you don't know King Travant. Prince Leaf had his parents and sister killed by Travant,","202":"(Levin (Strategist)): and in a way utterly unbecoming of a knight, too. Don't let your guard down — he's surely scheming something...","203":"(Travant): Hehehe... so Bloom is dead. That sweeps away the Empire's power here entirely.","204":"(Travant): Alright, now's our chance. First, we'll take Manster.","205":"(Travant): Altena, go with Coulter and take Manster.","206":"(Travant): If anyone resists, show no mercy even to civilians — kill them all!","207":"(Altena): Please wait, father! If the enemy is the Empire, I'll fight gladly, but killing powerless civilians is meaningless.","208":"(Altena): We ought to be able to cooperate with the Liberation Army — why must we fight them!","209":"(Travant): Altena! Are you trying to lecture me? You should just do as I say. I won't tolerate any back-talk!","210":"(Altena): But...","211":"(Arion): Altena, do as father says. Father and I must return to the capital to prepare for the next battle.","212":"(Arion): You're the only one who can hold the front line.","213":"(Altena): Brother... understood...","214":"(Travant): Now that you understand, stop dawdling! Go!!","215":"(Travant): Altena finally set out, did she... what a strong-willed girl.","216":"(Travant): Her mother too was a woman of strong spirit. Blood doesn't lie, I suppose.","217":"(Arion): Father, Altena means no harm. Please, go easy on her.","218":"(Travant): I know that already! Arion, let's return to the Thracian capital.","219":"(Travant): We'll lead a great army and take the whole peninsula in one stroke.","220":"(Travant): Mycoff, I leave Miloah Castle to you. Hold it to the death, together with Altena, until we return!!","221":"(Mycoff): Yes sir, understood.","222":"(Villager (man)): Lady Sety, this is terrible! Thracia's dragon knight corps has set out from Miloah Castle, heading for this castle.","223":"(Sety): What? After we finally took the town back from the Empire's rule,","224":"(Sety): has King Travant finally revealed his true colors!","225":"(Villager (man)): The Liberation Army hasn't crossed the river yet. Whatever should we do?","226":"(Sety): All of you, please flee to Conote. For a while, at least, I'll hold off the enemy by myself.","227":"(Villager (woman)): Lady Sety, that's impossible. Holding them off alone, something like that... you'll die!","228":"(Sety): I was prepared for this from the start. But don't worry — I won't go down so easily.","229":"(Sety): Now, there's no time left. Please, go quickly!","230":"(Villager (woman)): Lady Sety...","231":"(Coulter): Lady Altena, what's wrong? Manster Castle is right before us — let's begin the attack at once.","232":"(Altena): Wait, Coulter... our opponents are just civilians. There's no need to kill them.","233":"(Altena): I'll talk to them, try to get them to surrender. Wait a little.","234":"(Coulter): That won't do. I've been firmly instructed by the king.","235":"(Coulter): No matter what you say, Lady Altena, we're not to loosen our attack.","236":"(Altena): I am the commander here. Are you saying you won't heed my orders!","237":"(Coulter): This is my unit. If you don't like it, Lady Altena, you may stay here and watch.","238":"(Coulter): We'll go on without you. All troops, charge! We'll kill every last one of them!","239":"(Altena): W-, wait! Coulter!!","240":"(Celice): Brave Sety, thank you for helping the townspeople.","241":"(Sety): Lord Celice... I have been waiting. Waiting for this moment to come, all this time.","242":"(Sety): Lord Celice, please save the world. So many people are in the depths of despair.","243":"(Sety): Even here in Manster, many children have been captured and sent off to the Temple of Miletos.","244":"(Sety): I... I couldn't save the children. I'm no hero. I'm nothing but a coward...","245":"(Celice): Sety, that's not true. I can't do anything alone either.","246":"(Celice): It's only with everyone's strength that I've come this far.","247":"(Celice): Brave Sety, I want your strength. Please, lend me your power.","248":"(Sety): Yes, Lord Celice... I will go with you, wherever that may be!","249":"(Mycoff): The rebels have reached Manster Castle, you say? Damn it... what on earth is Lady Altena doing!","250":"(Mycoff): There's no helping it — all troops, strengthen our defenses! We'll hold this castle to the death, until Lord Travant returns!!","251":"(Sety): Ah, Lord Celice!? ...and who is the one at your side...?","252":"(Celice): Hey there, Sety. He's Levin, my strategist.","253":"(Sety): Levin... so it really was you, father...","254":"(Levin (Strategist)): Sety, so you've noticed, have you. It's been a long time — are you well?","255":"(Sety): Don't ask if I'm well!! I've been searching for you this whole time.","256":"(Sety): Do you have any idea how many years it's been since you left our country!","257":"(Levin (Strategist)): Come to think of it, how many years has it been? Is Fury doing well?","258":"(Sety): How can you... mother has passed away!","259":"(Sety): Before she died, she wished so badly to see you, even just once, that I set out on a journey to find you, father.","260":"(Levin (Strategist)): I see... so Fury... that's a terrible thing to have happened...","261":"(Sety): Father, you're a cold man. Even hearing of mother's death, you don't shed a single tear...","262":"(Levin (Strategist)): .........","263":"(Sety): Fee resented you too. She decided she wouldn't speak to you herself.","264":"(Sety): Surely you must know why, father — why don't you ever reach out to her?","265":"(Levin (Strategist)): Sety, I have neither wife nor child — that's the decision I made. You should think the same of yourself...","266":"(Sety): Father...!?","267":"(Fee): Sety... you're my brother Sety, aren't you!","268":"(Sety): You're... Fee!? What's wrong! Why are you here?","269":"(Fee): I came looking for you, brother. Because you left Silesse and never came back!","270":"(Sety): I'm sorry... while I was searching for father, I ended up drifting here to Manster,","271":"(Sety): and the people of this country were just too pitiable, so I couldn't bring myself to leave...","272":"(Fee): That's so like you, brother... it's alright, I love that about you.","273":"(Sety): Have you joined the Liberation Army?","274":"(Fee): Yes, I wanted to be of help to Lord Celice.","275":"(Sety): I see... you really are mother's child too, after all...","276":"(Sety): It seems you can't just stand by and watch when someone's in trouble.","277":"(Fee): You're just as much that way yourself, brother... but poor mother Fury — I can't forgive father!","278":"(Sety): Father, huh... that man really is a mystery. I wonder what he's thinking, deep down...","279":"(Femina): Brother... you're brother Hawk, aren't you!","280":"(Hawk): You're... Femina!? What's wrong! Why are you in a place like this?","281":"(Femina): I came looking for you, brother. Because you left Silesse and never came back!","282":"(Hawk): I'm sorry... while I was searching for the old man, I ended up drifting here to the kingdom of Manster,","283":"(Hawk): and the people of this country were just too pitiable, so I couldn't bring myself to leave...","284":"(Femina): That's so like you, brother... it's alright, I love that about you.","285":"(Hawk): Have you joined the Liberation Army?","286":"(Femina): Yes, I wanted to be of help to Lord Celice.","287":"(Hawk): I see... Femina, you've admired Lord Sigurd ever since you were small, haven't you.","288":"(Femina): Yeah, me, I always dreamed of becoming a pegasus knight like Lady Fury.","289":"(Femina): Watch me, brother — I'll do my best, okay!","290":"(Mana): Lord Celice...","291":"(Celice): Ah, Mana, what's wrong?","292":"(Mana): Lord Celice, I'm scared. When we left Isaac, I said such big, confident things,","293":"(Mana): but watching everyone fight like this, I keep thinking someone's going to end up dead...","294":"(Celice): Mana...","295":"(Mana): Lord Celice, did you see that female mage? She vanished in the blink of an eye.","296":"(Mana): I feel like some evil power beyond our imagination is at work.","297":"(Celice): ...Mana, to tell you the truth, I'm scared too. There are nights I'm too frightened to sleep...","298":"(Celice): If I could, I think I'd just want to run away from this whole world. But you know, Mana, I won't run.","299":"(Celice): You saw the people of Alster, and of Conote, didn't you.","300":"(Celice): When we liberated those towns, everyone wept with joy — that's how terrible the Empire's rule truly was.","301":"(Celice): I can't just leave the world as it is. We have a duty to save its people.","302":"(Mana): ...Lord Celice, I'm sorry for worrying you. I'll be alright now. I'll do my best too.","303":"(Mana): But please, don't push yourself too hard either — if you died, it would all be for nothing...","304":"(Celice): Thank you, Mana. I need you with me...","305":"(Mana): Lord Celice...","306":"(Celice): Tinny, do you know Princess Ishtar?","307":"(Tinny): Yes, Lady Ishtar always doted on me like a little sister.","308":"(Celice): I wonder who that boy was, the one who came to fetch her.","309":"(Tinny): Probably... Prince Julius.","310":"(Celice): What, Prince Julius!?","311":"(Tinny): Yes, the two of them love each other deeply. That's why he came for Lady Ishtar...","312":"(Celice): You know Prince Julius?","313":"(Tinny): I met him a few times in the capital, Belhalla. How should I put it...","314":"(Tinny): He has a strange power that draws people in, and... an icy coldness. A frightening man.","315":"(Tinny): He hardly seems human at all...","316":"(Nanna): Are you Ares?","317":"(Ares): Yeah, that's right. What do you want with me?","318":"(Nanna): I heard you're the son of King Eltshan — is that true?","319":"(Ares): That's right, but why do you ask?","320":"(Nanna): Ahh, so it really was true! I'm Nanna — the daughter of Lachesis, King Eltshan's younger sister!","321":"(Ares): Wh-, what did you say!? You're saying you're my aunt's daughter!","322":"(Nanna): Yes, mother has been worried about you this whole time.","323":"(Nanna): I believe part of the reason we came to Leonster was to search for you too.","324":"(Ares): My father, foreseeing that Agustria would fall into chaos,","325":"(Ares): entrusted my sickly mother and young me to our relatives in Leonster.","326":"(Ares): But then Leonster too was invaded by the Empire, and amid the flames of war, my mother died...","327":"(Nanna): And that's when Jabarro found you?","328":"(Ares): Yes, he took me in and raised me. I've traveled the world ever since, together with his mercenary company.","329":"(Nanna): So that's why we couldn't find you... Ares, there's something Mother Lachesis entrusted to me for you.","330":"(Ares): Hm? ...wh-, what is this? ...my father's...!?","331":"(Nanna): Yes, it's a letter addressed to you, from King Eltshan.","332":"(Ares): ! .........wh-, what is this...","333":"(Nanna): There, you see? King Eltshan trusted Lord Sigurd right up to the very end.","334":"(Nanna): I believe the two of them were truly close friends.","335":"(Ares): So that's how it was... I... I seem to have been mistaken...","336":"(Nanna): Ares, please protect Lord Celice. We need your strength!","337":"(Ares): ...understood, Nanna.","338":"(Ares): I'll teach you swordsmanship. Watch closely and see just what I can do.","339":"(Leaf): Hm? ...what's that I see over there — a Thracian lady dragon knight! ...but somehow, her eyes look so sad...","340":"(Villager (man)): Lord Celice's Liberation Army? You finally came!!","341":"(Villager (man)): Thank goodness, we're saved!","342":"(Villager (man)): Lord Celice, hooray!","343":"(Villager (woman)): Ahh, warrior... thank you so much!","344":"(Villager (woman)): Please, I beg you — help Lady Sety.","345":"(Villager (woman)): Thracia's dragon knights are attacking — please, be careful...","346":"(Coulter): Hehehe... sorry, but you'll have to die.","347":"(Coulter): Glory to Thracia! ...guh...","348":"(Mycoff): This land is ours. I won't let the likes of you take it from us.","349":"(Mycoff): Hooray for Thracia! ...guh...","350":"(Celice): Levin, the Thracian army is completely different from every enemy we've faced so far.","351":"(Celice): What are they fighting so desperately for, I wonder.","352":"(Levin (Strategist)): Thracia is an unblessed land.","353":"(Levin (Strategist)): Most of the country is harsh mountains, crops barely grow at all, and even making a living is far from easy.","354":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's why the men go off to war as mercenaries, and even the women must take on hard labor.","355":"(Levin (Strategist)): King Travant may be a dishonorable man, but he isn't fighting only for his own sake.","356":"(Levin (Strategist)): The soldiers of Thracia swear loyalty to their king because they believe he, and he alone, can save them.","357":"(Celice): I see... so that's why they fight so fiercely...","358":"(Levin (Strategist)): But even so, that doesn't make it right to invade other nations.","359":"(Levin (Strategist)): Travant's sense of justice belongs to Thracia alone,","360":"(Levin (Strategist)): and to the people of the peaceful northern peninsula, he's nothing but a hated invader.","361":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, I know it's painful, but we can't afford to loosen our grip here.","362":"(Levin (Strategist)): We will bring down the Thracian royal family, and build a peaceful nation where everyone in this region can help one another.","363":"(Levin (Strategist)): That is the mission given to us.","364":"(Altena): Even Miloah has fallen!? Was I... was I the one who was wrong... brother.........","365":"(Villager (man)): I hear the people of Manster Castle are planning an uprising too.","366":"(Villager (man)): Their leader is a young mage named Sety. He seems to be from Silesse, but the people adore him deeply.","367":"(Villager (man)): But Manster is also being targeted by Thracia — I wonder if it'll be alright.","368":"(Villager (woman)): Ahh, thank you so much.","369":"(Villager (woman)): Ever since I heard rumors of the Liberation Army, I've been waiting for this day to come — Lord Celice is the light of our hope!","370":"(Villager (woman)): As thanks, please accept this Power Ring. I hope you'll keep it with you.","371":"(Villager (woman)): Thracia and Leonster were once a single country, long ago.","372":"(Villager (woman)): But at some point, they came to hate each other... I wonder why they couldn't live together in peace.","373":"(Auntie): Thracia has coveted this region for a long, long time.","374":"(Auntie): Each time, the Leonster royal family took up the holy lance Gaebolg and protected us.","375":"(Auntie): But that Gaebolg, along with Lord Quan, Lady Ethlyn,","376":"(Auntie): and then Lady Altena's own life, vanished into the Yied Desert...","377":"(Elder): The kingdom of Thracia was founded by the dragon knight Deen.","378":"(Elder): He wielded the heavenly lance Gungnir, and fought against the Demon King.","379":"(Elder): They say the holy knight Nova, ancestor of the Leonster royal family, was Deen's younger sister...","380":"(Old woman): Ho ho, to think you'd come all the way out here — you must be quite the curious one yourself.","381":"(Old woman): Well, since you've come all this way, let me give you something good.","382":"(Old woman): This is called the Thief's Bracelet — a strange bracelet that grants the wearer a thief's skill.","383":"(Old woman): Ho ho ho, take good care of it."};
